# Trivy ignore file for Honryu security scanning
# This file contains security findings that are acceptable for our use case

# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS is now configurable via build args
# and can be set to empty in security scanning contexts
DS002

# Allow HEALTHCHECK absence - we rely on Kubernetes health checks
DKL-DI-0005

# Allow latest tag in development contexts (not production)
DKL-DI-0001

# Allow privileged operations in build stage only
DKL-DI-0002

# Allow ADD instead of COPY for remote URLs in JMeter download
DKL-DI-0010

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kubernetes misconfiguration checks (deploy/chart/honryu)
#
# Everything below is a capability the platform cannot function without, so
# these are accepted rather than fixed. The security-context findings that
# *were* fixable (KSV-0118, KSV-0014, KSV-0012, KSV-0001, KSV-0104, and the
# capability/seccomp set) are deliberately absent from this list -- they were
# closed by adding real pod and container securityContexts, not silenced.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# RBAC: the scheduler adapter's Role is the platform's job description. It
# creates and tears down engine workloads on demand, so each of these verbs
# is exercised by internal/adapters/scheduler/k8s/k8s.go directly:
#   KSV-0056 (services: delete)  -- engine Service teardown, k8s.go:594
#   KSV-0048 (pods/statefulsets) -- engine pods are the product
#   KSV-0049 (configmaps)        -- per-run engine config
#   KSV-0113 (secrets)           -- BYOC cluster credentials
# Narrowing any of them would break load generation. The Role is already
# namespace-scoped; the only cluster-scoped grant is nodes:list.
KSV-0056
KSV-0048
KSV-0049
KSV-0113

# Private registry: images come from registry.pve.heri.life, which is not in
# Trivy's default trusted-registry allowlist and cannot be. Pulling honryu's
# own builds from honryu's own registry is the intended design, and every
# tag is pinned explicitly (values.yaml image.*) rather than floating.
KSV-0125

# MySQL runs as uid/gid 999, below the 10000 these two want. That is the uid
# the mysql:8.4 image defines and the uid every file in the live datadir is
# already owned by -- remapping a populated database to satisfy a numeric
# range check would be real risk for no real gain. The honryu binaries, which
# had no such constraint, use 10001 and do not trigger these.
KSV-0020
KSV-0021
